    "explanation": "To both parties, on trip TRP-02820.\n\nDistance. The governing figure is the GPS trace distance, and EV-GPS-02820 records 4.04 km against the booked optimal of 3.2 km (EV-TRIP-02820) — an excess of 0.84 km, or 26.25% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (more than 20% and more than 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. The trace is clean for policy purposes: 46 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) does not fire, the finding stands on the trace alone, and no independent corroboration is needed. The trace figure governs over the rounded 4.0 km on the trip record.\n\nRefund. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 applies and the refund is arithmetic. Charged total is $9.70. The recomputed optimal-route fare is ((3.80 + 0.75 x 3.2 + 0.28 x 6.0) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + $0.00 ERP = (3.80 + 2.40 + 1.68) + 0.80 = $8.68; the surge multiplier of 1.0 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier (EV-FARE-02820), not from the trip record. Refund = 9.70 - 8.68 = $1.02, which is above the $0.50 de minimis floor and well below 90% of the charged total, so the payable amount rounds up to $1.05. Ruling: PARTIAL_REFUND of $1.05.\n\nThe driver's 'One-way streets'. This is a general traffic assertion with no advisory identifier cited. No traffic advisory is on file: EV-ADVIS-02820-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. The POL-RD-03 comparison therefore cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 the assertion carries no weight and reduces no excess. Because no advisory ID was cited, this is a gap in the bundle rather than the contradiction that would escalate under POL-RD-10(5), so the case is not escalated on that ground.\n\nThe remaining clauses. No rider-requested detour: the chat log (EV-CHAT-02820) carries 0 messages, so POL-RD-04 excludes nothing. No pickup or dropoff amendment is recorded and the vehicle type is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 do not apply. The repeat-deviation test in POL-RD-06 fails (deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 408 completed trips in 90 days; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a near-synonym and is not the field this clause names), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. There are no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines on this fare, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct and there is no billing-integrity referral; the off-route ERP total of $0.00 is not added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. No driver compensation is due: the billed distance (4.0 km) is within 1.0 km of the trace distance, so POL-RD-04's compensation limb does not fire. The rider's profile does not impose extra corroboration (deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the trigger of 4), and the rider's POL-RD-08 burden is discharged on matching trip IDs and the threshold excess.\n\nConfidence is capped by the weight of the artifacts that carry the deciding facts — the GPS trace and trip record for the deviation, the fare breakdown and trip record for the arithmetic — all at weight 1.0 — and is set at 0.95, above the 0.70 escalation floor, so no escalation arises. The monetary effect ($1.05) is below the $8.00 automatic execution threshold and will be executed automatically. No referral is made."
