    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the arithmetic, and the record is clean, so this is decided on the measured figures.\n\nDEVIATION. The governing distance is the GPS trace polyline for trip TRP-02820: 4.04 km against a booked optimal of 3.2 km — an excess of 0.84 km, or 26.25% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (the excess is greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own trace. The excess is not a MATERIAL deviation (below 50% and below 8.0 km). The trace is unimpaired: 46 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0, so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) does not fire, no independent corroboration is needed, and POL-RD-10(3) gives no ground to escalate on trace integrity.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. 'One-way streets.' cites no artifact. Under POL-RD-13 such an assertion is tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else, and the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-02820-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) — no advisory covers the Blk 12 Telok Blangah Cres corridor in this window. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot be run, the excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and because the driver cited no advisory identifier this is a gap in the bundle, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. Two rider claims to this same effect were discarded at the citation stage for not naming the missing artifact's issue code; the surviving version names it and is accepted.\n\nNO OTHER EXCUSE. No distance is excluded on any other ground: the chat log carries 0 messages, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable (no rider instruction, no waypoint_hint); pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 cannot run; and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The booked optimal of 3.2 km stands as the baseline.\n\nTHE MONEY. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs and the refund is arithmetic. The surge multiplier is 1.0, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier. recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 3.2 + 0.28 × 6.0) × 1.0 = 7.88, plus the 0.80 platform fee and 0.00 ERP = 8.68. charged_total is 9.70, so the refund is 9.70 − 8.68 = 1.02, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05 = 1.05. That is above the 0.50 de minimis floor and far below the 90% full-refund share (8.73), so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 1.05.\n\nNOTHING ELSE MOVES. The fare breakdown carries zero ERP gantries, zero tolls and a 0.00 airport surcharge on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct and no billing-integrity referral arises. POL-RD-06 is consulted because the deviation is established, but the pattern test fails: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 408 completed trips in 90 days, so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. prior_deviation_flags is a lifetime counter and is context only under POL-GEN-01; it is not used. No driver compensation is due under POL-RD-04: the billed distance (4.0 km) falls short of the trace (4.04 km) by 0.04 km, far below the 1.0 km threshold. The rider's profile does not require extra corroboration (deviation_claims_60d is 1, below 4).\n\nConfidence rests on the GPS trace, trip record and fare breakdown, each at weight_multiplier 1.0. The monetary effect of SGD 1.05 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue. This is a provisional ruling and either party may appeal it once under POL-GEN-04."
